    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Asking how someone is",
     "texto": [
      "**Apa kabar?** is the usual phrase for asking \"how are you?\" (or \"how are things?\"). Even though **apa** means \"what\" and **kabar** means \"news\", in this situation it doesn't translate literally as \"what news?\"."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Everyday forms of address",
     "texto": [
      "**Bapak** and **Ibu** are used to address adults respectfully; they can also mean \"father\" and \"mother\". **Mas** and **Mbak** are everyday forms of address for men and women, respectively, depending on the relationship and the situation. They don't always equal English \"Mr.\" and \"Mrs.\"."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
